# One vector-only scene through two profiles, each a 100x100 view: a red circle (r 20) with an ink outline at (50,50), over a soft gold halo (a gold circle r 26 at 80% opacity, blur 8).
# profile_modes_svg.svg (profile:svg) is an SVG, rasterized: red circle, ink outline, and a gold glow that fades out smoothly around it.
# profile_modes_raster.png (profile:raster) shows the same picture drawn directly. In both the halo is round and fades out, with no hard edge, and the circle outline is crisp.
# There is no profile:vector target: for a vector-only scene it writes the same bytes as profile:svg, so a second view would lock nothing new.
@artboard 100x100
@target targets/profile_modes_svg.svg profile:svg
@target targets/profile_modes_raster.png profile:raster

circle 26 at:50,50 fill:p.gold a:.8 blur:8
circle 20 at:50,50 fill:p.red stroke:p.ink,2
